     "content": {
      "text": "<p style=\"text-align:left\">How can preprint servers attract reviewers?</p>"
     },
     "elementId": "Google Shape;96;p18",
     "elementType": "text"
    },
    {
     "bounds": [
      41.94,
      78.39,
      621.59,
      290.17
     ],
     "content": {
      "fontFamily": "Open Sans",
      "text": "<p style=\"text-align:left\">Default to open licenses and formats, so as to allow </p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">reposting</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">reusing</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">repackaging</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">Make it easy to find out which aspects of a preprint are most in need of review</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">Make it easy to annotate preprints by </p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">having HTML versions and </p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">enabling Hypothes.is</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">which can also be used for tagging</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">Replace tracking tools like DISQUS with non-tracking ones for commenting</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">Make it easy to subscribe to content alerts using specific filters, e.g. </p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">mentions of concept X in section Y, e.g.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">a particular cell line in the methods section</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">a specific author or institution in the article metadata</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">a specific set of papers or datasets cited in the reference section</p>\n<p style=\"text-align:left\">preprints/ papers with high similarity to a given piece of text (similar to <a href=\"https://jane.biosemantics.org/\">JANE</a>)</p>"
     },
